---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergenceHeader from '../../components/EmergenceHeader.astro';
import EmergenceFooter from '../../components/EmergenceFooter.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Architecture — The Fourth Branch | The Emergence Institute"
  description="How the Lattice works: a decentralized synthesis network running on hardware you control. Node tiers, the Georgist engine, and the path from your workstation to the Fourth Branch."
>
  <EmergenceHeader slot="header" />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">The Fourth Branch · Reference Architecture</p>
      <h1>The Lattice</h1>
      <p class="sub"><em>A decentralized synthesis network that runs on hardware you control.</em></p>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="intro">
        The Lattice is not a cloud service and it is not a blockchain. It is a network
        of physical nodes — running on workstations, homelabs, and single-board
        computers — that coordinate through peer witnessing, deterministic sortition,
        and ratification. No central servers.
        No extractive middleman. The hardware requirements are documented,
        the protocol is open, and the smallest viable node fits on a Raspberry Pi.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/join.html" class="btn btn--filled">Join the Lattice →</a>
        <a href="/emergence/updates" class="btn">See What's New →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STACK -->
  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="label gold">The Stack</p>
      <h2>Three layers, one substrate</h2>
      <p class="muted layer-intro">
        Every node runs the same three layers. What changes between a Raspberry Pi
        and a dual-GPU workstation is only how much synthesis work the node can carry.
      </p>
      <div class="layer-stack">
        <div class="layer-card">
          <p class="layer-num gold">Layer 1</p>
          <h3>The Node Backend</h3>
          <p>
            The substrate itself — a Rust peer node you build and run on the hardware
            you control. The node registers with the network, syncs state, and — once
            enough independent peers are present — begins participating in consensus.
            A node's identity today is a persistent Ed25519 key held on disk;
            hardware-held keys (TPM) are a planned direction so identity can never
            be silently impersonated.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="layer-card">
          <p class="layer-num gold">Layer 2</p>
          <h3>The Georgist Engine</h3>
          <p>
            The economic core — "Attention as Land." Information that sits idle decays;
            active contribution is what holds value. Resources are priced by use, not
            hoarded. It is a Georgist framework expressed directly as running code.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="layer-card">
          <p class="layer-num gold">Layer 3</p>
          <h3>Witnessed Consensus</h3>
          <p>
            Contributions are ratified by a witness panel selected through deterministic,
            contribution-weighted sortition, and committed to an append-only hash chain.
            The durable consensus and authority layers are still under development, and
            end-to-end liveness across multiple nodes does not yet pass. The earlier
            "Proposer / Opposer / Synthesizer" framing was conceptual design language —
            it is not how the running engine reaches consensus.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NODE TIERS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="label gold">Hardware Tiers</p>
      <h2>Find your node</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Three tiers, defined by the hardware you already have. You can start as a Leaf
        today and grow into a Trunk as your participation deepens.
      </p>
      <div class="tiers-grid">
        <div class="tier-card">
          <div class="tier-icon">🌱</div>
          <h3>Leaf</h3>
          <p class="tier-hw gold">Raspberry Pi · single-board</p>
          <p>
            The entry point. A Leaf node participates in consensus, relays state, and
            keeps the network honest. Low power, always on, fits on a shelf.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-card">
          <div class="tier-icon">🌿</div>
          <h3>Branch</h3>
          <p class="tier-hw gold">Homelab · mid-range GPU</p>
          <p>
            A working node. Branches carry real synthesis load, peer with the discovery
            network, and serve as local coordination points for a cell.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-card tier-card--featured">
          <div class="tier-icon">🌳</div>
          <h3>Trunk</h3>
          <p class="tier-hw gold">Dual-GPU workstation · Ampere</p>
          <p>
            The heavy lifter. Trunk nodes resolve consensus across the distributed
            network and run the validation layer at scale. The reference
            Trunk runs on a dual RTX 3060 (Ampere) configuration.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE PATH -->
  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="label gold">From Workstation to Network</p>
      <h2>The path a node walks</h2>
      <div class="path-steps">
        <div class="path-step">
          <p class="step-label gold">Step 1 · Register</p>
          <p>Get the node software and generate a persistent identity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-step">
          <p class="step-label gold">Step 2 · Provision</p>
          <p>Install and run the node, verify your hardware, and bring the synthesis engine online in your chosen tier.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-step">
          <p class="step-label gold">Step 3 · Peer</p>
          <p>Your node connects to the discovery network and begins syncing state with the rest of the Lattice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-step">
          <p class="step-label gold">Step 4 · Synthesize</p>
          <p>Trunk nodes resolve consensus; the Georgist engine prices resources; the validation layer processes its cycles.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-step">
          <p class="step-label gold">Step 5 · Steward</p>
          <p>The network reaches into the physical world. Local hardware monitors local resources — the architecture made real.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PHYSICAL PILOT (DESIGN) -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="label gold">Designed, Not Yet Deployed</p>
      <h2>The Urban Water Loop</h2>
      <p class="intro">
        A design for the architecture's first physical deployment: a local cell
        monitoring aquifer levels and infrastructure through the Triadic Witness
        protocol — community hardware watching community resources. No extractive
        middleman, no centralized sensor network. When deployed, this would put
        "Attention as Land" into practice: finite resources tracked by the people
        who depend on them.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/emergence/protocols" class="btn">Read the Design →</a>
        <a href="/emergence/charter" class="btn">Read the Charter →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="label gold">The Work Is Open</p>
      <h2>The mesh capability exists. The full architecture is still being built.</h2>
      <p>
        Run a node on hardware you control, inspect the engineering specifications, or
        contribute to the build — a decentralized network that asks for neither crypto
        nor cloud dependency.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/join.html" class="btn btn--filled">Join the Lattice →</a>
        <a href="/spec.html" class="btn">Protocol Spec (One-Page) →</a>
        <a href="/books" class="btn">Read the Books →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TECHNICAL REFERENCE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="label gold">Go Deeper</p>
      <h2>Lattice Technical Reference</h2>
      <p class="intro">
        See the implemented protocols, current development state, and engineering
        specifications behind the architecture.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="https://themycelium-lattice.netlify.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn">Open the Technical Reference →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">In This Section</p>
      <div class="arch-links">
        <a href="/emergence/lattice-spec"><strong>Lattice Specification</strong><span>The full wire-and-consensus spec</span></a>
        <a href="/emergence/lattice-substrate"><strong>Lattice Substrate</strong><span>The 13-layer cryptographic boundary</span></a>
        <a href="/emergence/constitutional"><strong>The Constitutional Room</strong><span>Ten immutable primitives</span></a>
        <a href="/emergence/tripartite-council"><strong>Tripartite Council</strong><span>Three co-equal branches</span></a>
        <a href="/emergence/trilateral-receipt-spec"><strong>Trilateral Receipt Protocol</strong><span>Three-party relay attestation</span></a>
        <a href="/emergence/ethical-hardware-enclave"><strong>Ethical Hardware Enclave</strong><span>HEIP — the isolated sandbox</span></a>
        <a href="/emergence/georgist-economics"><strong>Georgist Economics</strong><span>The economic layer of the Lattice</span></a>
        <a href="/spec.html"><strong>Protocol Spec</strong><span>The one-page summary</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EmergenceFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .sub {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 660px;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .layer-intro {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .layer-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .layer-card {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
  }

  .layer-num {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .layer-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }

  .layer-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .tiers-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .tier-card {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .tier-card--featured {
    border-color: var(--gold);
  }

  .tier-icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .tier-card h3 { margin: 0; }

  .tier-hw {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-family: monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .tier-card p:last-child {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .path-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .path-step {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .path-step:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .step-label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .path-step p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .cta-row { flex-direction: column; }
  }

  .arch-links {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .arch-links a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .arch-links a:hover {
    border-color: var(--gold);
  }

  .arch-links strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .arch-links span {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
